+- **ShopConstraint semantics (multishop, #41568).** Every value read/write takes a `ShopConstraint` and honors all its shapes. **Writes fan out**: a shop-group / all-shops / `ShopCollection` constraint upserts one row per shop in scope for per-shop storage (`isMultiShop()` tables), batched into a single multi-row UPSERT per table — native ObjectModel parity (`ExtraPropertyWriter` resolves the scope via `Core\Shop\ShopListResolver`, whose group/all scopes only contain usable shops: `deleted = 0 AND active = 1`, like `Shop::getContextListShopID()`). **SHOP-scope rows follow the native association rule**: broad scopes (group/all) only refresh shops the entity is associated with in `{entity}_shop` (a later-associated shop reads the definition default until the next save), while explicitly named shops (single shop, `ShopCollection`) always get their row; LANG rows cover the full scope regardless of associations, like native lang-multishop writes. **Reads pin one deterministic shop**: single-shop → that shop; otherwise the constraint's *representative* shop (default shop when in scope, else lowest id) — the same rule the BO/API context listeners now use to set `ShopContext::getId()`, so grid pinning and reader agree. **Toggle** reads the representative value and writes its inverse to every shop in scope (uniformizes divergence); LANG toggles need a `langId`. The constraint's `isStrict` flag is meaningless here (no group/global storage rows) and is ignored. Legacy side: `Context::getShopConstraint()` maps `Shop::getContext()` (all/group/shop) and `ObjectModel::persistExtraProperties` follows `$id_shop_list` via `ShopCollection`; `ObjectModel::delete()` calls `deleteForShops()` on partial (per-shop) deletion and `deleteAll()` on full deletion.
 - **`ExtraPropertiesBag`** is the single lazy resolver for both `ObjectModel::$extra_properties` and FO lazy arrays; it dirty-tracks writes. ObjectModel persists modified values in `add()`/`update()` via `persistExtraProperties()`. FO arrays opt in via `AbstractLazyArray::initExtraPropertiesBag()` (Product, Category, Manufacturer, Supplier, Store, Order, OrderDetail, OrderReturn, Cart). FO vs BO is **auto-detected** inside `createForEntity()` via `Context::isFrontOfficeContext()` (fallback `_PS_FRONT_DIR_`): FO reads see only `display_front = 1` fields, BO/CLI/API see all — so native `$entity->extra_properties` access is FO-safe with no module code.
 - **Identifier safety contract.** The `ExtraPropertyDefinition` constructor validates `entityName`, `propertyName` and the computed storage column as SQL identifiers (≤64 chars), so DDL consumers embed them in SQL without re-validating. `entityName` is normalized to snake_case (`tableize()`) at construction.
 
